    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town grew into a shipping hub when the Powell Valley Railroad arrived in 1887, linking it to Norfolk Southern.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luttrell%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Luttrell sits in a valley between Copper Ridge to the north and Clinch Mountain to the south, part of the Appalachian Ridge‑and‑Valley range.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luttrell%2C_Tennessee"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Flat Creek, a tributary of the Holston River, drains the city’s landscape.",
